        <p>There is still some chance, I hear, of Prince Louis Battenberg becoming a successful inventor. The aavY has for many years sought a signalling appar- atus ter ? and Prince Louis (who is a captain in the pt vice), in conjunction with Captain Percy Scott, ....oduced a highly ingenious instrument, which was rjerimented with during the recent manceuvres. ia,,B()lue respects it proved unsuitable, and many everts preferred an apparatus invented by Admiral 4". which had the manifest advantage of being 4oilable at night. The Battenberg-Scott invention purrever, is superior in some vital points, and the nee is now engaged in introducing improvements t",i,.tla a view to further trials. Briefly, this appara- is a diamond-shaped cone attached to the mast- and divisible into three parts. It is worked riY Pulleys from the deck, and a code has been made ,cla combinations of the three parts which -4ables signals to be exchanged at a distance of ten</p>
