        <p>PROGRESS is being reported in Tbe Canal. connection with the Ship Canal, diffi It is now said that many of the —culties with the railway companies which vseverely handicapped the Canal Company in de- Ping traffic have been removed, and it is in sequence anticipated that there will be in the diate future a large expansion of business. hat will be good news forth° canal shareholders for the ratepayers of Manchester. It is, of ituirB9, well known that two or three of the large Ivay companies who are interested in the Man- , Zaster trade did not look with a kindly eye upon ect.e eatal, and they did not spare either money or the'rta to frustrate the scheme for making Man- .l.2ter a seaport. But the canal is now a great and even railway directors find that facts are ebb orn things which cannot be disputed. The Panies have not up to the present displayed undue zeal in providing facilities for the trans- ellee of goods from the Manchester but if it be true that more cordial robs- have been formed between :the canal and ZwaY authorities an additionol impetus should given to the growth of traffic. The London ti North:Western Railway Company are now 48Yeonstructing a branch line connecting their *lle. naive system with the Manchester docks at a between Patricroft and Mode Wheel, and 12 Lancashire and Yorkshire Company have also Zeontracts with the view of securing direct corn- -,•;ll4ication with the docks. IR other respects the 'aual Company and others concerned are acting IPParently in the confident expectation of a great ''lll4:rease of traffic. At Manchester and Salford , ot'Wards of thirty miles of railway have been laid a°Wilt and in other respects it is said that = torircithing that science and ingenuity can devise I the rapid and effective handling of goods 11)pe ars to have been overlooked." It is claimed "Ilat the series of fireproof warehouses are more ;(41arklete and commodious than any that can be in any other port in the kingdom, while the e' of buildings upon which the Manchester '11i1) 0 anal Warehousing Company are spending Iviuu,ooo are rapidly approaching completion. It 11 ide seen, therefore, that, in spite of all it:"itaistic forebodings, there is still plenty of 1111 in the ultimate success of the canal.</p>
