        <p>NEW TALE! NEW TALE!! A SENSATIONAL NEW TALE, ENTITLED:- " THE HIDDEN HAND; OR CAPITOLA THE MADCAP," BY MRS. E. D. E. N. SOUTH WORTH. WILL BE COMMENCED IN THE "F AXAMINER" OF OCTOBER 19TH. This tale is one of the most opular stories ever issued from the press. We doubt if, in oil the realms of literature, there has ever hen a he eine who could vie with the captivating madcap Capito!a in exciting the admiration ot readers, or in wit,ning ad keeping their hearts. She is so bright. so spirited, so beautiful, so sagacious, so dauntless, and yet so innocent and childlike that she at once takes all readers cap- tive and holds them enchained by her f .scinatious clear to last page of the story. The way C .pi tole outwits, overcomes and capttres the gigantic and brutal robber Black Donald, wt« n he had concealed himself in her lonely room at the dead night, it one of the mst thrilling chapters in the entire range of romantic literature.</p>
