        <p>AUSTRALIAN CRICKET TEAM TO VISIT ENGLAND. A Dalziel's cablegram, dated Sydney. Oct. 9, states:— The Australian Cricket Council has decided to send a team of cricketers, representing the three principal colonies, to England in the spring of next year. Methods have been adopted with a view to securing better dis- cipline among the members of future teams than was the case in some of the previous organisations. Mr. Alcock, of the Surrey Club, has been asked to arrange a series of matches for the Australian players. The tour also em- braces a trip to America, where a number of matches will be played.</p>
